{"repositoryId":1348024766,"availability":"available","full":"BeniCheni/kickoff","name":"kickoff","description":"⚽ Big-5 European football fixtures + standings, in Brooklyn time. Generated and diffed, never typed — a tracker whose house rule is: never a confident lie. Built as a partner-in-crime project with Claude Code.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-27T03:25:33Z","updated":"2026-10-12T23:47:46Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["ai-assisted-development","bundesliga","claude-code","fixtures","football","la-liga","ligue-1","premier-league","react","serie-a","soccer","standings","typescript","vite","zod"],"demo":"https://benicheni.github.io/kickoff/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:20.818Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:20.818Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:20.818Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T23:51:20.818Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["[]( [](CHANGELOG.md) [](LICENSE) [](CLAUDE.md) []( [](docs/moments-player-plan-review.md)","A football fixtures tracker that would rather admit what it doesn't know than tell you a confident lie — and an open notebook on how one person ships software with three AI vendors building, reviewing and rebutting each other's work.","You don't need to follow football to read this repo. The football is the excuse. The interesting part is the workflow: every line of the app was written by an AI coding agent, every pull request is cold-reviewed by a different vendor's agent, the builder gets to argue back in writing, and a human rules on whatever is still contested. The paper trail for all of it is in this repo, PR by PR."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/BeniCheni/kickoff/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0affe4272fe064961bd0e257b50e7b48a3f36903ba742500a4eefbea6c80a947","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T23:51:20.966Z"},"overviewChec